      "evidence_grounding": "Strong - Directly supported by evidence linking thalamus to task execution (E1, E4), PCC to decision-making (E1, E4), and sleep disruption reducing thalamocortical coupling (E2, E3). Insomnia severity (ISI) is explicitly validated as a biomarker (E1-E4).",
      "graph_consistency": "High - Thalamocortical coupling is explicitly supported by 12 findings (e.g., E3: 'increased VMHC in thalamus/posterior insula'), and thalamus-DMN FC is linked to cognitive domains (E1, E4).",
      "mechanism_specificity": "High - Focuses on thalamocortical coupling, a specific mechanism with clear neural correlates (thalamic connectivity, thalamic radiation).",
      "plausibility": "High - Thalamocortical coupling is a core sleep-regulating network; its disruption aligns with known cognitive deficits in insomnia.",
